                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "45756896",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197991043929",
                            "num_reviews": 45,
                            "playtime_forever": 233,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 61,
                            "last_played": 1699144670
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Four of us played Tile Battle locally in Big Picture Mode with controllers. We were initially skeptical as our first match was mostly a long-winded stalemate.\n\nHowever, we gradually began to better understand the game mechanics and to develop strategies. The first map is also tight, but the subsequent maps are a bit larger and it helped open up some potential tactics. \n\nThe game has a bit of a tower defense feel, though not exactly. You basically place up to five arrows on the map to direct your army to destroy the enemy base. At the same time, you need to misdirect the enemy army away from your own base with those same arrows. It is a simple idea that requires some surprising amount of strategy. \n\nUltimately, all four us ended up enjoying the game and we played a few matches in a row. Tile Battle is unique and I think it will be on our rotation for a while.",
